 | Bugbot | Bugbot comments on a GitHub PR are ordinary review threads, so triage them with the forge command that the step gives. Skip a step that starts, waits for, or configures Bugbot when the PR has no Bugbot check or comment. |
 | Cursor cloud agents | `environment: "cloud"` maps to a worktree, as in Subagent fields. Skip a step that needs the cloud agent itself, such as its dashboard status or its own machine. |
 | A built-in PR tool | Use the forge command that the step gives, such as `gh pr create`. That is not a skip, so write no line. |
+| `control-ui`, `control-cli`, or any skill from `cursor-team-kit` named as the control skill | The project's own control skill, a project-local skill under `.claude/skills/` that drives the app the way a user does. If the repo has none, run the **create-verification-skill** skill once to make it. Until one exists, drive the surface through the project's own runner (its test command, a headless or scripted run, a screenshot tool the session has) and say which. That is not a skip, so write no line. |
+| `/deslop` from `cursor-team-kit` | Claude Code's built-in `/simplify` over the diff, then remove what it leaves of narrating comments, unsupported guards, dead compatibility paths, and unrelated edits. That is not a skip, so write no line. |
